  "question": {
    "text": "For the solution of the gases&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math> in water at <math><mn>298</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the Henry&#39;s law constants <math><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.5,</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>35</mn></math> and <math><mn>40</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>,</mo></math> respectively. The correct plot for the given data is:"
