  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub></math></p><p>Where, <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub></math> is the partial pressure of gas.</p><p><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></msub></math> is&nbsp;the Henry&rsquo;s constant</p><p><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub></math> is&nbsp;the mole fraction of gas</p><p><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></msub></math></p><p>On comparing this with the equation of straight line,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>mx</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math>, the intercept,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></msub></math>. Thus, the gas having more value of Henry&#39;s law constant will have more value of intercept on the y-axis.</p>"
